  <static seed="223" source="Contrib/Valdosta/APEX_Calculus/2.5/APEX_2.5_13.pg">
    <statement><p>Compute the derivative of the given function.</p>
<p><me>f(x) = 11 \sec(12 x)</me></p>
<p><m>f'(x) =</m><fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>132\sec\mathopen{}\left(12x\right)\tan\mathopen{}\left(12x\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> Solution:</alert> 



Use the Chain Rule with inside function <m>u = 12 x</m>
and outside function <m>y = 11\sec u</m>.



<me>\begin{array}{rcl}
    f'(x) \amp =\amp  \displaystyle\frac{dy}{du} \cdot \frac{du}{dx}\\
    \amp \amp \\
    \amp =\amp  (11\sec u \tan u)(12) \\
    \amp =\amp  132 \sec(12 x)\tan(12 x)
  \end{array}</me>


</solution>
